Two tests that still assert the host instead of the contract
================================================================

Both of these passed on a desktop and failed in the Arch CI image. Neither failure was a bug in
the platform layer: the tests were asking whether the machine looked like a developer's machine,
which is the exact defect 0011 removed everywhere else.

1. `installed_apps_are_well_formed` asserted "more than ten applications". A container ships no
   .desktop files at all, so the suite was unpassable there for no product reason. The contract is
   that whatever is found parses and carries a usable Exec line; an empty menu is a real
   environment, and it now says so and returns.

2. `a_bare_session_reports_every_backend_it_tried` asserted the error names spectacle or grim. On a
   host with neither installed the error names the backends that ARE present, so the test failed
   exactly where the layer was working correctly. It now accepts any backend name the layer can
   try, which is what it was always trying to say.

Neither test is weakened: on a normal desktop they still validate every entry and still require an
error that names what was attempted.

--- a/crates/quixi-platform/tests/compat_desktops.rs
+++ b/crates/quixi-platform/tests/compat_desktops.rs
@@ -189,8 +189,16 @@
     // `which` falls back to the standard bin directories, so a tool that is installed
     // on the host is still attempted here — what matters is that the failure names
     // what was tried instead of returning a bare "capture failed".
+    // Any of these may be the one this host actually has. What the contract requires is that the
+    // error names what was tried instead of a bare "capture failed" — naming only spectacle/grim
+    // made this pass on a desktop and fail in a container, which is the same host assumption the
+    // rest of this patch exists to remove.
+    const TRIED: [&str; 9] = [
+        "kwin-screenshot2", "portal", "gnome-shell-screenshot", "spectacle", "grim",
+        "xfce4-screenshooter", "cinnamon-screenshot", "gnome-screenshot", "import",
+    ];
     assert!(
-        err.contains("capture") && (err.contains("spectacle") || err.contains("grim")),
+        err.contains("capture") && TRIED.iter().any(|b| err.contains(b)),
         "the error should name the backends it tried; got: {err}"
     );
 }
